  "final_text": "The September photo changes two fields on the bank form. **F2 (electricity use) goes from GAP to COVERED at 320.9 MWh**, which also makes the **F3 share calculable at 56.1 %**. F4 stays at 5.0 years, and F1, F5 and F6 stay GAP because none of the files cover them.\n\n**Checking the invoice itself (invoice-EL-25-09.png):** it covers 01.09.2025–30.09.2025, meter FICT-0001. The meter readings are 1.284.350 → 1.325.550, so 1,325,550 − 1,284,350 = **41,200 kWh**, which matches the quantity line (\"41.200\" in German/Macedonian number format = 41,200). 41,200 kWh × 9.50 MKD/kWh = 391,400 MKD, which matches the total due. The invoice is internally consistent. It is stamped \"КОПИЈА\" (copy), but it's an issued supplier invoice with measured readings, so I accept it as evidence.\n\n**What changes**\n\n| Where | Before (value, status) | Now (value, status) | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F2 Electricity 2025 | 279.7 MWh, only 11 months. **GAP**: September missing | **320.9 MWh, COVERED** | 279,700 + 41,200 = 320,900 kWh across 12 unique months. September (41,200 kWh) was the highest month of the year. |\n| F3 PV yield and share | 180 MWh. Share couldn't be calculated (or would have been a wrong 64.4 % on 11 months). **GAP** | 180 MWh, **56.1 %** of 2025 use. **WEAK** | 180,000 / 320,900 kWh. The yield is the installer's estimate in an unsigned offer, so it must be marked as an estimate. |\n| F4 Payback | 5.0 years, WEAK | 5.0 years, WEAK (unchanged) | 8,550,000 MKD / (180,000 kWh × 9.50 MKD/kWh). The September invoice confirms the same 9.50 tariff. Still based on the unsigned offer. |\n| F1, F5, F6 | GAP | GAP (unchanged) | The invoice doesn't touch fines, staff or certificates. |\n\n**Bank form**\n\n| No | Question | Answer | File and line | Status | Reason | Missing document | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | Fines 2023–2025 | – | – | GAP | No file | Confirmation of environmental, labour and H&S fines 2023–2025 (or a signed \"none\" statement) | Request it |\n| F2 | Electricity 2025 | 320.9 MWh | electricity_2025.csv lines 3–14; invoice-EL-25-09.png (readings, quantity) | COVERED | 12 months, kWh checked against the readings | – | Remove the duplicate October line (line 12) and book EL-25-09 in the CSV |\n| F3 | PV yield and share | about 180 MWh/yr (**estimate**), 56.1 % | solar_offer_2026.txt lines 8, 11; F2 | WEAK | Installer's estimate, offer signed by neither side | Signed offer or yield report | Mark it as an estimate on the form |\n| F4 | Payback | 5.0 years (**estimate**) | solar_offer_2026.txt lines 8–9; electricity_2025.csv line 3 ff. (9.50) | WEAK | Built on the unsigned offer | Signed offer | Mark it as an estimate on the form |\n| F5 | Employees and accidents 2025 | – | – | GAP | No file | Average headcount 2025 from payroll, accident register 2025 | Request them |\n| F6 | Certificates and audits | – | – | GAP | No file | Valid certificates or audit reports with the next audit date | Request them |\n\nCount: 1 COVERED, 2 WEAK, 3 GAP.\n\n**Other points to note**\n- **Duplicate in the CSV:** October 2025 (EL-25-10, 38,700 kWh) is entered twice, on lines 11 and 12 (e-invoice and scan). It's counted once above. Summing the CSV rows naively gives a wrong total.\n- **The offer expires soon:** it's dated 2 September 2026 and valid for 60 days, so until about 1 November 2026. It's still valid on 16 October, but the bank may need the signed or extended version.\n- Filling the September gap with an average would have been wrong: 11 months × 12/11 gives 305.1 MWh, and the true total is 320.9 MWh.\n\n**Request (by number of fields)**\n1. Signed solar offer / yield report: F3, F4\n2. Fines confirmation 2023–2025: F1\n3. Average headcount and accident register 2025: F5\n4. Valid certificates or audit reports: F6\n\nA person still needs to review and sign the form before it goes to the bank.",
